 "circuits": [
  {
   "id": "decoupling",
   "title": "Supply decoupling and pin connections",
   "page": 12,
   "description": "The supply pin VDD3.3V is bypassed to GND by five capacitors in parallel, 1 nF, 2.2 nF, 10 nF, 47 nF and 1 µF, set on the bottom layer between pins 4 and 6 or on the top layer beside pins 4 and 5. CLKIN takes the reference clock; 1Y0 to 1Y3 drive the clock loads. CLKOUT runs only a very short way to delay-tuning capacitor pads whose value follows the load on the outputs; it drives no trace. A full reference plane runs under the clock lines to their receivers.",
